==Battleground==
*1 [[Doge]] spawns after 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
*1 [[Flying Ninja Cat (Enemy)|Flying Ninja Cat]] spawns as the boss.

==Strategy==
One thing about this stage overall is that you're definitely going to want to bring [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating Cats]] like [[Delinquent Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Angry Delinquent Cat]], [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sadako Cat]], [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] or [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Necro-Dancer Cat]]. Take advantage of the fact that [[Flying Ninja Cat (Enemy)|Flying Ninja Cat]] is a [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemy. Additionally, meatshields are a must.

If you have Sadako Cat, this stage is ridiculously easy. Just bring Sadako Cat, Necromancer Cat, and any cheap damage dealer, such as [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]]. All you have to do is spam Sadako Cat and Necromancer Cat. The boss cannot advance, as it will be frozen and weakened. Dragon Cat is just there to make this fight a bit faster.

Similarly to Sadako Cat, [[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Freshman Cat Jobs]] can make this stage ridiculously easy. Outranging Flying Ninja Cat, it can consistently weaken it to nearly no damage while your attackers whittle it down.

If you have no anti-Floating Cats that can help against Flying Ninja Cat, bring 4-5 meatshields, a few attackers with >240 range, and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]] or a similar [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]].

